\newlabel{fig:qft}{{4}{16}{Quantum circuit implementing the Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT). The output states are shown unnormalized (the $1/\sqrt {2}$ factors are omitted). Controlled phase shift gates $CR_k$ are represented by phase shift gates $R_k$ acting on the target qubit, with filled dots indicating their respective control qubits. Notice how by reading the output qubits downwards, we obtain the QFT in the reversed order, so a final SWAP gate is required in order to obtain the desired result}{Doc-Start}{}}
